# Package Scripts — Keep Minimal

Allowed `package.json` scripts (do **not** add others without an explicit user request):

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `test` | Full BDD pipeline + Playwright. Filter with `-g` |
| `bddgen` | Generate specs only (no test run) |
| `audit:csv-coverage` | CSV ↔ feature coverage audit |

## How to run tests

```powershell
yarn test -g "@module-tag"          # e.g. @agency-dashboard, @smoke
yarn test -g "@TEST-AGD-001"        # single scenario
yarn test -g "@TAG" --retries=0 --reporter=line  # debug — never omit --retries=0
yarn test -g "@smoke" --headed      # headed
yarn test --ui                      # Playwright UI mode
yarn bddgen                         # generate only
```

Extra args after `yarn test` are appended to `playwright test`.

## Do NOT add

- Per-module aliases (`test:agency-dashboard`, `test:smoke`, …)
- Headed/UI/cucumber variants (`test:headed`, `test:cucumber:open`, …)
- One-off explore/debug wrappers — run `node scripts/….mjs` directly if needed

When documenting or invoking OpenCode, use `yarn test -g "@<tag>"`, never `npm run test:<module>`.
